    "done_when": "One integration measurement of the fast CPU suite at the merged head of this wave, judged by delta against the base before the wave, reported only: no repository path is written. Base revision 7c4a76cafa41f4f5a4da06af19a0f0aac3271560 (main before the topology read, kernel repair, tuple and doubles landings); head revision ec7fef752 or newer main at dispatch (the run's orientation_base_sha). Done when: (1) the fast suite (the path-free default, which excludes slow-marked tests) is run once at the base revision and once at the head, each as ONE SLURM job on all_debug (srun --partition=all_debug --time=00:59:00 --cpus-per-task=8 --mem=64G, export TMPDIR=/tmp, JAX_PLATFORMS=cpu, the shared environment's interpreter /home/ITER/mcintos/Code/nova/.venv/bin/python run directly with PYTHONPATH set to the tree under test, never uv on the compute node), with pytest-xdist -n 8 and a per-test timeout of 600 s, the base tree obtained as a git archive of the base revision extracted under /tmp on the node (the extraction removed at the end), each run captured to one log under the run directory; (2) the manifest's baseline_suite and after_suite record revision, command, exit_status, log_path, completed true, failure_count and failure_ids as module-qualified node ids (the module path and test name joined by two colons, as pytest prints them) read from the logs' FAILED and ERROR lines; (3) the manifest and the report name every added failure id (in the head, not in the base) with its traceback's first error line, every removed failure, and the expected-failure counts, so the coordinator can attribute each added failure to a landing; zero added is the pass and a nonzero count is reported, never repaired here; (4) if the suite aborts mid-module (one process SIGABRT killing the session, which this repository's CPU lane has shown), rerun that module alone in a fresh process and record the module, so an abort is never reported as a pass or as failures of the modules after it. Negative control: an injected test file under the run directory with one deliberately failing test, collected in a separate short pytest invocation through the same id-extraction script, must appear as an added failure id in that script's output, proving the delta instrument reports a failure it is shown. Every uv command on the login node carries --no-sync and nothing runs uv sync; configure_dtypes() is not this node's concern since no code is written. Commit nothing to the repository; the manifest, logs and report are the delivery.",
    "estimated_hours": null,
